# Everything here is measured, not guessed. Before this file grew the entries
# below, `COPY . /app/` shipped 616 MB and the `chown -R` after it wrote the
# whole tree a second time -- 1.2 GB of a 2.76 GB image, none of it reachable.
#
# A leading `**/` matters: a bare pattern anchors to the build-context root, so
# `.pytest_cache` did not match the nested `backend/.pytest_cache` that was in
# the shipped image.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# Local virtualenvs. The one on this machine is 581 MB of macOS/aarch64 CPython
# ("home = /Library/Frameworks/Python.framework" in its pyvenv.cfg) and it was
# being copied into a linux image that already has its own venv at /opt/venv.
# It could never have run; it was pure weight on every push, pull and deploy.
.venv
venv
**/.venv

# Celery beat's shelve database. Beat runs with WORKDIR=/app and no --schedule
# flag, so it opens `celerybeat-schedule` relative to the working directory --
# meaning a copy baked in from a developer's machine is what a fresh container
# reads its last-run times from. Runtime state, never build input.
celerybeat-schedule*

# Runtime output, not source: WAREHOUSE_AUDIT_DIR's manifests and the
# collectstatic target (a named volume mounts over it in compose anyway).
recovery-manifests
staticfiles

.env*
tests
graphify-out
.git
.DS_Store
